+# F-30: Tend UI Queue Tabs
+
+## Result
+
+Status: `[x] complete`
+
+The queue/status selector now renders through Tend UI `Tabs` with six accessible queue tabs and the existing dynamic counters.
+
+## Ownership Contract
+
+React owns only the visual tabs, selected indicator and rendered count labels.
+
+S-Tracker vanilla modules remain authoritative:
+
+1. React emits `s-tracker:queue-request` with a validated status key candidate.
+2. `src/features/tasks/tasks-view.js` confirms the status through `src/domain/queue-state.js`.
+3. Vanilla code renders tasks, pagination, detail counts and sidebar totals.
+4. Vanilla code calculates every queue summary with the active navigation and filters.
+5. Vanilla code emits `s-tracker:queues-changed`.
+6. React synchronizes the selected tab, counts and overdue indicator.
+
+The adapter contains no mock-task generation, filter rules, navigation matching, pagination or direct `renderTab` call.
+
+## Public Package Export
+
+F-30 exposed the existing Tabs component through a narrow package path:
+
+```text
+@10d/tend-ui/primitives/Tabs
+```
+
+The export provides ESM, CJS and type entrypoints. The main package, local tarball and S-Tracker lockfile were refreshed offline.
+
+## Preserved Product Contract
+
+| Scenario | Verified result |
+| --- | --- |
+| Queue labels | Six accessible Tend UI tabs |
